    {
      "id": "s10",
      "short": "Recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "body": "• **Polling** — Delay: Up to the interval; Direction: Client asks\n• **Long polling** — Delay: Low; Direction: Client asks, server waits\n• **SSE** — Delay: Low; Direction: Server → client\n• **WebSocket** — Delay: Lowest; Direction: Both ways\n\nPersistent connections need many servers at scale, joined by **pub/sub**. **Store** every message first, so offline users catch up when they return.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "That completes Communication. Next module: **Reliability** — starting with redundancy and failover."
      },
